# SSH-Chatter Multi-Protocol Integration Configuration Example
# This file demonstrates how to configure Matrix, IRC, and FidoNet integrations

# ============================================================================
# IRC Configuration (e.g., for magviz.ca)
# ============================================================================
# Uncomment and configure these to enable IRC relay

# CHATTER_IRC_SERVER=irc.magviz.ca
# CHATTER_IRC_PORT=6667
# CHATTER_IRC_CHANNEL=#general
# CHATTER_IRC_NICKNAME=ssh-chatter-bot
# CHATTER_IRC_USERNAME=chatbot
# CHATTER_IRC_REALNAME=SSH-Chatter IRC Bridge

# ============================================================================
# Matrix Configuration
# ============================================================================
# Uncomment and configure these to enable Matrix bridge
# Note: You need to create a bot account and generate an access token first

# CHATTER_MATRIX_HOMESERVER=https://matrix.org
# CHATTER_MATRIX_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_matrix_access_token_here
# CHATTER_MATRIX_ROOM_ID=!roomid:matrix.org
# CHATTER_MATRIX_DEVICE_NAME=ssh-chatter

# ============================================================================
# FidoNet/Binkp Configuration (e.g., for magviz.ca)
# ============================================================================
# Uncomment and configure these to enable FidoNet relay

# CHATTER_FIDONET_SERVER=magviz.ca
# CHATTER_FIDONET_PORT=24554
# CHATTER_FIDONET_ADDRESS=2:5030/1997
# CHATTER_FIDONET_PASSWORD=your_session_password

# ============================================================================
# Notes
# ============================================================================
# 
# Matrix Setup Steps:
# 1. Create a bot account on your Matrix homeserver
# 2. Login with Element or another client
# 3. Go to Settings → Help & About → Advanced → Access Token
# 4. Copy the token and set it as CHATTER_MATRIX_ACCESS_TOKEN
# 5. Create or join a room and copy its ID (starts with !)
# 6. Set CHATTER_MATRIX_ROOM_ID to that room ID
# 7. Restart ssh-chatter
#
# IRC Setup Steps:
# 1. Choose an IRC server (e.g., irc.magviz.ca)
# 2. Decide on a channel to join (must start with #)
# 3. Set the configuration variables
# 4. Restart ssh-chatter
# 5. Use /ircserver status to check connection
#
# FidoNet Setup Steps:
# 1. Obtain a FidoNet node address from your network coordinator
# 2. Get the hostname/IP and port of your hub (usually port 24554)
# 3. Get your session password from the hub administrator
# 4. Set the configuration variables
# 5. Restart ssh-chatter
# 6. Use /fidonet status to check connection
#
# Operator Commands:
# - /ircserver status|reconnect|disconnect
# - /fidonet status|reconnect|disconnect
# (Matrix commands coming soon)
#
# Messages will appear with prefixes:
# - [IRC] for messages from IRC
# - [FidoNet] for messages from FidoNet  
# - [matrix] for system messages from Matrix
